// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded base-10 exponential 10^x of F16
//
// x = x1 + x2, where x1 keeps the upper 11 bits of the encoding and x2 the sign, the exponent and the lower 5 bits:
// 10^x = 10^x1 10^x2, both tabulated as F32 values whose product rounds correctly to F16. Round to nearest only:
// overflow gives +inf, underflow +0, NaN comes back quiet.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary16/exp10/exp10f16.c via RazorForge's B16Exp10.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2025 Maxence Ponsardin and Paul Zimmermann
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

